  concept: "Authored objective: Safe Backup LED Current.\nAuthored requirement: BACKUP
    snapshot: 2-12 mA flowing through the 330 ohm LED limiting resistor. current
    \u2265 2 mA. current \u2264 12 mA. Connection pair R_LED_Input and R_LED_Output.\nGeneral
    teaching principle: An LED has a defined anode and cathode; correct polarity
    and suitable current control matter for normal forward operation.\nOnly fresh,
    authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A directional gate with a current limit is a useful model, although an
    LED is not an ideal one-way switch.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A lit LED alone does not establish that its current and power are
    within safe ratings.
